 "note": "MIXED PAGE: it continues the three columns ELEMENTARY | MIDDLE | HIGH begun on page 21 and prints no school name or column headings of its own. It holds 35 high, 34 elementary and 30 middle entries, so it is filed under the high school (a one-entry margin over elementary; the elementary column is the Passios faculty, its principal on page 21 being William F. McSheehy, named Passios principal in the 1991 report, page 60). Each entry's grade_or_dept starts with its column (ELEMENTARY:, MIDDLE:, HIGH:) and then the section label above it, carried over from page 21 where the section began there (VandeWater continues KINDERGARTEN; Gillham's GRADE 6 starts on line 1). Textract rebuilt rows across columns that do not share baselines, so columns were assigned by each column's own sequence and by the order of cells within each row; single-name rows were placed by continuity and are the least certain: Philip Crouse/Jean Koykka (5, 7) HIGH MATHEMATICS, Margaret Curley (12) HIGH ENGLISH, Kathleen McGuigan and Kay Hillman (25, 28) HIGH FOREIGN LANGUAGE (both under Foreign Language in 1993), Michelle Harvey (52) HIGH SCIENCE, Ronald Lamothe (59) HIGH SOCIAL STUDIES. Two PHYSICAL EDUCATION headings at lines 35 and 36: the one at the end of line 35 is read as HIGH (Dunigan, Stachowicz follow) and the one on line 36 as MIDDLE (Diamantopuolos, Leserte). GRADE 8 is printed twice in the middle column (lines 17 and 20); all five names under them are recorded as GRADE 8. Headings kept as printed, including the OCR forms 'SPERCH' and 'COMPUTER COODINATOR'. The middle column's PRINCIPAL'S ADVISORY COUNCIL (lines 56, 58, 60-61, 63-64, 66-70: Cringan, Kearns, Falcone, Bourque as staff members, then parents) and the high column's PARENT ADVISORY COUNCIL (lines 69-74) are councils, not staff: none of their names is recorded; lines that hold only council names plus a staff heading are in headings, lines 69-74 are ignored. There is no page number line."
